-- title:
--   Connecting sum Theta: linearity, coboundaries, equivariance, peeling
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$, and let $X_0$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $k$: a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $F = X_0.F$ together with series $[a] = X_0.\mathrm{act}\,a$ for $a$ in the Witt ring $\mathrm{Zp2}\,q = \mathrm{WittVector}\ q\ (\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2)$ and a series $\Pi = X_0.\mathrm{varpi}$, all endomorphisms of $F$ in the sense of `IsLawHom`, with the usual multiplicativity, additivity, $\Pi\circ\Pi = [q]$ and $\Pi\circ[a] = [a^{\sigma}]\circ\Pi$ relations. Two operations on power series are introduced: $\mathrm{pull}\,\varphi\,\Gamma = \Gamma(\varphi(X),\varphi(Y))$, obtained by substituting into $\Gamma \in k[[X_1,X_2,Y_1,Y_2]]$ the two-block family built from $\varphi$ in the left and in the right variables, and $\Theta\,\Gamma = \sum_{i=0}^{q-1}\Gamma([i]X, X)$, where $[i] = F.\mathrm{nthSeries}\ i$ is the iterated sum series ($[0]=0$, $[n+1] = F([n]X,X)$). The assertion is a conjunction of six statements: (i) $\Theta(c\Gamma+\Gamma') = c\,\Theta\Gamma + \Theta\Gamma'$ for $c \in k$; (ii) if $g$ has zero constant term then $\Theta(\partial g) = g([q]X)$, where $\partial g = g(F(X,Y)) - g(X) - g(Y)$ is `addCoboundary`; (iii) $\Theta(\mathrm{pull}\,[a]\,\Gamma) = (\Theta\Gamma)\circ[a]$ for every $a$; (iv) likewise $\Theta(\mathrm{pull}\,\Pi\,\Gamma) = (\Theta\Gamma)\circ\Pi$; (v) if $\Gamma$ is a symmetric normalised two-cocycle for $F$ (zero constant term, invariance under interchanging the two blocks of variables, and the cocycle identity in three blocks) then $\partial(\Theta\Gamma) = \Gamma([q]X,[q]Y)$; (vi) for any $\varphi$ with all constant terms zero and any $\Gamma$ with zero constant term, $\mathrm{pull}\,\varphi\,\Gamma$ lies in the ideal generated by the four series $\varphi_i(X), \varphi_i(Y)$.
--
--   These are the defining properties, written on representatives of power series, of the connecting map from symmetric two-cocycles of $F$ (extensions of $F$ by $\mathbb G_a$) to homomorphisms $F[q] \to \mathbb G_a$: items (ii) and (v) say that $\Theta$ is well defined modulo coboundaries and lands in the primitive elements modulo $([q])$, while (iii) and (iv) record exact commutation with the $\mathcal O_D$-action. The package is used in the proof of [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.exists_eq_addCoboundary_of_subst_varpi_eq_addCoboundary_of_coeff_eq_zero`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.exists_eq_addCoboundary_of_subst_varpi_eq_addCoboundary_of_coeff_eq_zero).
